# Canvas auto-fit rules

The fitter (`FitTextToViewportCoreAsync` → `TrySizeAsync` → `ProbeFit`) binary-searches font size.
One false "overflow" signal makes it shrink to the floor (`MinScaleFactor` = 65%), and the scene ends up
with text in the top half and an empty bottom. Every rule below exists to stop false overflow signals.

## Overflow detection
- Vertical overflow is decided by the scroller (`ExtentHeight > ViewportHeight`) and by the last glyph's
  bottom vs `ActualHeight - Padding.Bottom`. Do not add other vertical signals.
- Horizontal overflow only counts when a glyph is **past** the edge: `right > LimitW + edge`.
  Never use `> LimitW - edge`. Canvas editors have zero horizontal padding, so right-aligned and
  justified lines end exactly at `LimitW`. That check flagged every right-aligned scene as clipped.
- Keep the phantom guard in `ProbeFit`: overflow with no scroll overflow, no width overflow, and
  slack > `PhantomSlackRatio` of the height is a measurement error, not overflow.
- Any new overflow check must hold for all four alignments (Left, Center, Right, Justify), all four
  typefaces, and both 96 and 108 base sizes. Right-aligned at 108 is the one that broke.

## Overflow: never crop, never cut a sentence
- Order is fixed: shrink to the largest size where the **last word** is visible, down to the floor.
  Only if the text still overflows at the floor, carry the rest onto a new screen.
- Every fit runs this check (`FitAndMaybeOverflowAsync`): no word-count gate, no typing-only flag.
  A scene left clipped at the floor is a bug.
- Pick the cut with `TryMeasuredSplit` (measures glyph positions at the floor size), not with word counts.
  Cut priority: sentence end (`. ! ? …` / newline), then clause (`, ; : —`), then word. Mid-sentence only
  when a single sentence can't fit on one screen.
- Carried text goes onto **one** new screen placed right after its source (`OpenOverflowScreenAsync`).
  That screen fits and splits on its own. Never pre-chunk carried text by word count.
- Word-count splitting (`TrySplitOverflow`) is only a packing heuristic and must snap to `PickBreak`.

## Measuring
- Never measure (probe, fit, `EditorTextOverflows`) between `editor.BeginUpdate()` and `EndUpdate()`.
  Layout is frozen there and the probe reads stale geometry. Call `EndUpdate`, `FlushEditorLayout`, then fit.
- Apply size with `ApplySizeOnly` across the whole story. Mixed run sizes make `CharacterFormat.Size`
  undefined, and the probe then logs `size=12` (the fallback).

## Diagnosing
- `fit-debug.log` lives in the package `LocalState`. Every fit line carries `page=<Id> align=...`.
- Bad-fit signature: `overflow=1 scroll=0` with large positive `slack` and `size` at the floor.
  Check the `width=` and `phantom=` fields to see which signal fired before you change thresholds.
- Fix the detector. Do not paper over it with per-scene size overrides or by raising the floor.
